    $seedie$Near our school gate stands a yellow lost-and-found box. Students put keys, scarves, and water bottles inside. Every Friday, Student Council members sort the things and post a short list on the notice board.

Last month I lost my blue scarf. I checked the box and found three blue scarves! I looked for a small star sticker on the label—my mum had put it there. That sticker helped me take the right one home.

The council also reminds us: write your name on cups and put valuable cards in zip pockets. Finding lost things feels good, but keeping things safe feels better. The yellow box teaches care and honesty at the same time.$seedie$,
