    'r07b-03',
    $seedie$Planting Trees on Tree-Planting Day$seedie$,
    $seedie$植树节种树$seedie$,
    7,
    'g7b',
    'ai_generated',
    $seedie$medium$seedie$,
    $seedie$nature$seedie$,
    $seedie$On March 12, our class went to East Hill to plant trees. Each group carried a young sapling, a bucket, and gloves. The soil was soft after spring rain.

First we dug a hole deep enough for the roots. Then we placed the sapling carefully and covered the roots with soil. We poured water slowly so it could sink down. Our teacher said roots need air too, so we should not press the soil too hard.

After two hours, twenty new trees stood in a line. We made wooden labels with the date and our group names. Some students joked that the trees would grow taller than us. I hope they grow strong and clean the air for people who walk on East Hill later.$seedie$,
