    $seedie$family_life$seedie$,
    $seedie$Sunday afternoon, Dad taught me to cook egg fried rice. We washed rice, cut spring onions, and beat two eggs. Dad said the pan must be hot before the oil goes in.

I poured the eggs too early and they stuck a little. Dad laughed and said mistakes are part of learning. We tried again. This time the rice jumped in the pan with a happy sound. We added peas and a little salt.

When Mum came home, she tasted a spoonful and gave a thumbs-up. The kitchen smelled wonderful. I wrote the steps in my notebook so I can cook again next week. Food made together tastes warmer than food bought outside.$seedie$,
